From 5519a1e9ac97ab394bc063d8c39a286ca2de6a10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: impl <impl@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:30:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fx: C versions of the matrix asm functions (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The MWCC inline asm (`asm void`) in lib/NitroSDK/src/fx/fx_mtx22.c,
fx_mtx33_identity.c, fx_mtx33_rot_yz.c, fx_mtx43_identity.c, fx_mtx43_rot.c,
fx_mtx43_scale.c, fx_mtx44_identity.c and fx_mtx44_rot.c does not parse under
GCC, so these eight files fail the port's GCC build. Each of the 14 functions
gets a plain C version under #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS, placed before the original
asm, which stays unchanged under #else. The DS (MWCC) build does not define
SDK_PORT_3DS and keeps the asm.

What each C version reproduces (decoded from the HGSS asm at the pin, 8cbb4a1):

- MTX_Identity22_, MTX_Identity33_, MTX_Identity43_, MTX_Identity44_:
  identity matrix, 1.0 as FX32_ONE on the diagonal, zero elsewhere, including
  the zero translation row of the 4x3 form.
- MTX_Copy43To44_(src r0, dst r1): copies the 4x3 into the first three columns
  of the 4x4. Fourth column is 0, except row 3, which is FX32_ONE.
- MTX_Copy44To43_(src r0, dst r1): copies the first three columns of each row,
  dropping column 3.
- MTX_RotX43_, MTX_RotY43_, MTX_RotX44_, MTX_RotY44_, MTX_RotZ44_,
  MTX_RotY33_, MTX_RotZ33_ (sin r1, cos r2): rotation in NitroSDK's row-vector
  convention. -sin is computed as 0u - (u32)sin, so INT32_MIN stays INT32_MIN,
  as the asm's neg does.
- MTX_Scale43_(x r1, y r2, z r3): diagonal (x, y, z), zero translation row.

Each asm function stores every element of its destination, and so do the C
versions. There are no multiplies or rounding steps: the asm stores, copies
and negates values only.

DS output is unchanged. Without SDK_PORT_3DS the preprocessed output
(gcc -E -P) of each of the eight files is identical to HEAD, and the diff
removes no line. The asm is kept byte-for-byte under #else.

Cross-check: Platinum's pokeplatinum-3ds patches/NitroSDK/0003 has C versions
of the same-named functions (different SDK revision). They agree with the
decoded HGSS asm. Platinum guards with SDK_CW/__MWERKS__; this patch uses
SDK_PORT_3DS, as the port's rule requires.

Verified with tests/sdk/fx/run.sh (host test, GCC -m32, 428 cases against the
definitions and literal outputs), and with an interpreter for the asm subset
(3011 checks against the definitions, including INT32_MIN/MAX inputs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
